# Day 38 – Typing Speed Studio

## Objective

The objective of today's experiment was to improve typing accuracy, speed, and consistency through an interactive typing practice application. The simulator focused on evaluating typing performance using different typing modes while providing detailed analytics to help identify strengths and areas for improvement.

---

## What I Did

In this experiment, I generated the Typing Speed Studio application as an HTML project and tested it in my browser. After answering the initial interview questions, I explored the available typing modes and completed multiple typing practice sessions.

During each session, I focused on improving my typing speed while maintaining accuracy. The application measured my typing performance in real time and provided detailed statistics after every practice session. I reviewed the Analytics Dashboard to analyze my typing speed, accuracy, consistency, and overall performance. To compare my results, I replayed the application using another typing mode and observed the differences in my performance. Finally, I captured screenshots of the important stages and documented the complete learning experience.

---

## Key Learning Outcomes

* Understood the importance of typing speed and accuracy in improving productivity.
* Learned how consistent typing practice helps develop better keyboard skills.
* Explored different typing modes designed to improve speed, accuracy, and consistency.
* Analyzed detailed performance metrics through the analytics dashboard.
* Improved my understanding of performance tracking using interactive web applications.
* Strengthened focus, hand-eye coordination, and typing efficiency through practical exercises.

